Why Identifying Vulnerabilities Matters for Phoenix
The reason we identify vulnerabilities separately from attacks is because one vulnerability can be the root cause of many different attacks at once. Fixing V14 for example the corrupted feedback vulnerability would protect Phoenix against adversarial feedback submissions, label flipping attacks, coordinated disinformation campaigns and agency impersonation all in one go. So instead of trying to defend against 78 individual attacks one by one the team can focus on fixing the 21 underlying vulnerabilities that make those attacks possible in the first place. That is a much smarter and more efficient way to build a genuinely secure system.

